1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mieszko cieszyński''' – od 1281/2 wspólnie z bratem Przemysławem w Cieszynie, Oświęcimiu i Raciborzu, od 1290 po podziale samodzielny '''książę cieszyńsko-oświęcimski'''. Założyciel linii Piastów cieszyńskich. [
2 CONC http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mieszko_cieszy%C5%84ski Wikipedia PL]
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mieszko_I,_Duke_of_Cieszyn
2 CONT
2 CONT Mieszko I Mieszko I Cieszyński seal 1288.PNG Mieszko I's seal, dated to 1288. Born	1252/56 Died	27 June 1315 Noble family	Silesian Piasts of Opole Spouse(s)	?Grzymisława Vsevolodovna of Belz Issue Władysław Casimir I Viola Elisabe
2 CONC th of Cieszyn Father	Władysław Opolski Mother	Euphemia of Greater Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue According to some sources,[1] Mieszko's wife died around 1303, but her name is unknown. The Obituary of the Church of St. Vincent in Wrocław showed the existence of a certain "Grzymisława, Duchess of Opole" (Gri
2 CONC mizlaua ducissa Opuliensis) who was buried there around 13 September 1286.[2] Her parentage is also unknown, but her name suggests a Russian origin, probably member of the Rurikids.[3] Her title suggests that she may have been the
2 CONC  wife of Mieszko I or the first wife of Bolko I (Mieszko I's brother), or maybe a completely different person.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, the exact date of their marriage was uncertain, but after a further reconstructions of their children's birth dates, was placed between 1275 and 1280. They had three children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Władysław (born 1275/80 – d. by 15 May 1324) Casimir I (born 1280/90 – d. by 29 September 1358) Viola Elisabeth (born ca. 1291 – d. 21 September 1317), married on 5 October 1305 to King Wenceslaus III of Bohemia __________________
2 CONC ________________________________________
2 CONT
