1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This (the children of Kasimir, Duke of Teschen) appears to be the generation in which Margaret is supposed to have emerged:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SILESIA.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT KASIMIR ([1276/80]-1358).  He succeeded as KASIMIR I Duke of Teschen.  After Jan King of Bohemia invaded Silesia in early 1327, he imposed Bohemian suzerainty on Duke Kasimir 18/19 Feb 1327[385].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1321/24]) EUPHEMIA of Mazovia, daughter of TROJDEN I Prince of Czersk [Piast] & his Maria Iurievna of Galich ([1310]-after 1373).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Kasimir & his wife had nine children: 
2 CONT *a)         ANNA ([1325]-1367).  The Chronica principum Polonie records that "Wenceslaus" married "ducis Theschnensis…filiam"[386].  m ([1338/40]) WENZEL I Duke of Liegnitz, son of BOLESLAW III Duke of Breslau, Liegnitz and Brieg 
2 CONC & his first wife Margareta of Bohemia ([1310/18]-2 Jun 1364).  
2 CONT *b)         WLADISLAW ([1325/31]-May 1355, bur Pisa Cathedral).  
2 CONT *c)         JOLANTA HELENA (-20 Mar 1364).  Abbess of St Clara in Krakow 1361. 
2 CONT *d)         BOLESLAW ([1331/32]-23 Jul 1356).  Canon at Breslau 1349.  He was chaplain to Emperor Karl IV.  Provost at Prague. 
2 CONT *e)         '''PREMISLAW von Teschen''' ([1332/36]-23 May 1410).  He succeeded as PREMISLAW I "Noszak" Duke of Teschen.  m ([1360/63]) ELISABETH von Beuthen, daughter of BOLKO Duke of Beuthen [Piast] & his wife Margareta von Stern
2 CONC berg ([1347/50]-after 1373).  Premislaw I & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT **i)          PREMISLAW ([1362/70]-murdered 1 Jan 1406).  He succeeded as PREMISLAW Duke of Auschwitz. 
2 CONT **ii)         BOLKO ([1363/74]-6 May 1431).  He succeeded as BOLKO I Duke of Teschen. 
2 CONT **iii)        ANNA (-after 8 Jul 1403).  m (before 29 Sep 1396) HEINRICH IX Duke of Haynau, Lüben and Ohlau, son of HEINRICH VII Herzog von Lüben und Brieg & his first wife Helene von Orlamünde ([1360/68]-[9 Jan 1419/10 Jul 1420])
2 CONC . 
2 CONT *f)          AGNES (1338-[6 Feb/27 Apr] 1371).  m ([1352/23 Feb 1354]) KONRAD II Duke of Oels, son of KONRAD I Duke of Oels [Piast] & his first wife Elisabeth von Breslau [Piast] ([25 Mar 1338/1340]-10 Jun 1403). 
2 CONT *g)         HANUŠ ([1339/40]-after 18 May 1359).  A priest.  
2 CONT *h)         '''SIEMOWIT''' (-[25 Sep 1391]).  Knight of the Teutonic Order.  Prior of Poland, Bohemia, Moravia, Austria, Styria and Carinthia 1372. 
2 CONT *i)          ELISABETH (-after 20 Jan 1364).  Nun at Treibnitz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT If Premislaw was her father, Medlands doesn't list her. If Siemowit was her father, then she must have been illegitimate.
2 CONT
