1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/federico-iv-d-aragona-re-di-sicilia-detto-il-semplice_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT  /!\ numbering II - III - IV  :  - https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federico_IV_di_Sicilia - fu Re di Sicilia (formalmente, Re di Trinacria), Duca di Atene e Duca di Neopatria, dal 1355 alla sua morte. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Federico''', come sovrano di Sicilia, avrebbe dovuto adottare il numerale '''III''', invece assunse il '''IV''', conformandosi alla scelta operata da suo nonno, https://www.geni.com/people/Federico-II-III-d-Aragona-re-di-Sicili
2 CONC a/6000000000153391275?through=6000000002372843490, che avrebbe dovuto adotare il numerale II, ma preferì il III, in omaggio a https://www.geni.com/people/Federico-II-Hohenstaufen-Sacro-Romano-Imperatore/6000000000424888017, che er
2 CONC a stato Re di Sicilia, ma che mai si disse Federico I di Sicilia. A ogni modo, in alcuni elenchi dei Re di Sicilia, Federico il Semplice è indicato con il numerale III. ('''Federigo II''' on MedLans Projects)
2 CONT ------
2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#FederigoIIdied1377 - FEDERIGO of Sicily (1 Sep 1341-Messina 27 Jul 1377).  Marchese di Randazzo.  He succeeded his cousin in 1355 as Duke of Athens and Neopatras.  He succeeded his brot
2 CONC her in 1355 as '''FEDERIGO II “il Simplo”''' King of Sicily, under the regency of his sister Eufemia of Sicily 1355-1357.  In 1357, faced with mounting opposition in Sicily, King Federigo proposed that Athens and Neopatras be tran
2 CONC sferred to his sister Leonor, wife of Pedro IV King of Aragon, in return for military help from the latter in Sicily, a proposal which was refused[428].  The dispute with the Anjou Kings of Sicily was settled at Aversa 31 Mar 1373
2 CONC , with Federigo allowed to remain in occupation in Sicily but with the title King of Trinacria.  Federigo II resisted pressure from Pedro IV King of Aragon, his father-in-law and brother-in-law, to assume greater power in Sicily a
2 CONC nd succeeded in having his daughter recognised as his heir.  
2 CONT *m firstly (Catania 11 Apr 1361) Infanta doña CONSTANZA de Aragón, daughter of don PEDRO IV “el Ceremonioso” King of Aragon & his first wife Infanta doña María de Navarra (Poblet 1340-Catania Jul 1363).  
2 CONT *m secondly ([17 Jan 1372/26 Nov 1373]) ANTONIA del Balzo, daughter of FRANCESCO del Balzo Duca d’Andria & his wife Marguerite di Tarento [Sicily-Anjou] (-23 Jan 1374, bur Messina). 
2 CONT *Mistress (1): ---.  The name of Federigo's mistress is not known.   King Federigo II & his first wife had one child:
