1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnim_VI._%28Pommern%29 Barnim VI, Duke of Pomerania From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT   (Redirected from Barnim VI) Barnim VI was duke of Pomerania-Wolgast from 1394 to 1405. He was the son of Wartislaw VI of Pomerania-Wolgast.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnim is known for his engagement in piracy. He erected a fort and a port for this purpose in Ahrenshoop, which was destroyed by Rostock in 1395. He allowed the Victual Brothers, a pirate organization assaulting vessels of the Ha
2 CONC nseatic League in the Baltic Sea, to use the Peene river as a winter refuge and the Bay of Greifswald as a basis. In 1398, he signed a treaty with the Teutonic Knights not to further support the Victual Brothers (then also "Likede
2 CONC elers"), but kept on engaging in piracy himself. On one of his expeditions, he was caught by the Hanseatic League in Kopenhagen's port. From 1400-1403, he aided the dukes of Mecklenburg-Werle in their campaigns against Lübeck. Bar
2 CONC nim himself was wounded once at Lübeck's gates.[1] In 1405, Barnim died of the Black Death. To avoid this fate, he went on a pilgrimage to Kenz near Barth, but died on his way. He was buried in Kenz, where a large wooden statue re
2 CONC sembling Barnim was furnished.[1] Diese Seite wurde zuletzt am 20. Oktober 2009 um 17:52 Uhr geändert Duke Barnim VI of Pomerania-Wolgast (1394-1405), *1365, +22.12.1405; m.Veronica N D1. Duke Wartislaw IX of Pomerania-Wolgast (14
2 CONC 05-57), *Wolgast 1400, +Schloss Darsim 17.4.1457; m.1420 Sophie von Sachsen-Lauenburg (*ca 1395 +1462) D2. Duke Barnim VIII of Pomerania-Wolgast, *1403/05, +21.7./20.12.1451 E1. Agnes, *1434, +Bernburg 9.5.1512; 1m: Tangermuende 9
2 CONC .2.1449 Friedrich I von Altmark-Priegnitz (*ca 1425, +Tangermünde 6.10.1463); 2m: 1479 Georg II von Anhalt-Zerbst (*1456 +25.4.1509)
