2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT By 10 February 1372, Rupert married with Hedwig (b. ca. 1350 - d. 27 March 1390), daughter of Henry V of Iron, Duke of Żagań and widow of King Casimir III the Great of Poland. They had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara (b. ca. 1384 - d. Trebitz, 9 May 1436), married on 6 March 1396 to Rudolph III, Duke of Saxe-Wittenberg and Elector of Saxony. Through this union, Rupert was a direct ancestor of the Kings of Denmark and the House of Gonza
2 CONC ga, rulers of Mantua and Montferrato.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (b. bef. 1385 - d. aft. 7 July 1411), a nun in Wroclaw.
