1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Infanta doña LEONOR de Aragón (Santa María del Puig 20 Feb 1358-Cuellar 13 Sep 1382, bur Toledo Cathedral).  Her marriage was arranged as part of the arrangements for peace with Castile agreed at Almazán 12 Apr 137
2 CONC 4 and at Lérida 10 May 1375.  She died in childbirth.  m (Soria 18 Jun 1375) as his first wife, Infante don JUAN de Castilla, son of don ENRIQUE II "él de las Mercedes" King of Castile & his wife doña Juana Manuel de Castilla Seño
2 CONC ra de Villena, Peñafiel y Escalona (Epila 24 Aug 1358-Alcalá de Henares 9 Oct 1390, bur Toledo Cathedral).  He succeeded his father in 1379 as don JUAN I King of Castile and León.  King Juan & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon, Queen of Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_of_Aragon,_Queen_of_Castile
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon (20 January 1358 – 13 August 1382) was a daughter of King Peter IV of Aragon and his wife Eleanor of Sicily. Her maternal grandfather was Peter II of Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her brother became Juan I, King of Aragon. She was born at Santa Maria del Puig and died at Cuéllar. On 18 June 1375, at Soria, she became Queen consort of Castile by marrying King John I of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their eldest son Enrique (1379–1406) became King Henry III of Castile and his younger brother Fernando (1380–1416) ultimately was elected to inherit Eleanor's native Aragon in 1412, becoming King Ferdinand I of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon
