2 CONT Barbara Celjska - Crna kraljica - poveznica na YOUTUBE VIDEO na Hrvatskom jeziku 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VpMW-nRyZvI
2 CONT
2 CONT Nemška in češka kraljica Barbara Celjska (1394? – 11. 7. 1445)
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara je bila najmlajša hčerka Hermana II. in Ane Schaunberške. Kot vsem drugim svojim otrokom, je Herman tudi njej v svojih načrtih za dvig rodu Celjskih pripravil posebno mesto, čeprav verjetno ni slutil, da bo prav Barbari us
2 CONC pel najvišji družbeni vzpon – ob bok cesarja Sigismunda Luksemburškega. Herman II. je delčke poročne "sestavljanke" verjetno začel sestavljati že kmalu po izgubljeni bitki s Turki pri Nikopolju (1396), ki bi se brez Celjanove pomo
2 CONC či lahko za Sigismunda tragično končala. Številnim izkazom hvaležnosti (posestim in počastitvam) je namreč leta 1405 sledila poroka Barbare Celjske in vdovca Sigismunda Luksemburškega, ogrskega kralja. Celjski so tako na najvišjem
2 CONC  mestu dobili "ambasadorja" in zagovornika svojih interesov, saj je Barbara z vsem srcem podpirala moževo naklonjenost do tasta in Celjskih nasploh (taka poteza je bil denimo sprejem Hermana II. in Friderika II. Celjskega v Zmajev
2 CONC  red – združbo najožjih kraljevih zaupnikov ter nenazadnje pokneženje).  Kronanje z nemško kraljevo krono v Aachnu (1414) in spremstvo moža na koncilu v Konstanci (1415) sta bila nekakšna vrhunca Barbarinega zakona s Sigismundom, 
2 CONC ki sta jima sledila razdor in prva (neformalna) ločitev leta 1419. Barbara je nato s hčerko Elizabeto (roj. ok. 1408) nekaj časa živela daleč proč od dvora in moža – sprva v okolici romunske Oradee, kasneje pa na Slovaškem (Malič)
2 CONC . Barbara je bila kasneje sicer dovolj pametna, da je moža prosila odpuščanja in dosegla vsaj navidezno normalizacijo odnosov. V 20. letih 15. stoletja se je intenzivno posvečala zaupanim državniškim zadevam – cesar ji je namreč p
2 CONC odelil razsežna ozemlja na Češkem in Slovaškem, ter skrbela za njihovo obrambo proti husitom. Konec husitskih vojn je zakonca spet začasno zbližal in Barbara je bila leta 1437 kronana kot češka kraljica. Sigismund je njuno hčer El
2 CONC izabeto leta 1422 poročil z Albrehtom II. Habsburškim, ki ga je podpiral v husitskih vojnah ter mu s hčerjo zagotovil tudi nasledstvo na rimsko-nemškem pr
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Barbara of Celje''' (Croatian and Slovenian '''Barbara Celjska'''; Hungarian '''Cillei Borbála''') or '''Barbara of Cilli''' (c. 1390/1395 – 11 July 1451) was Holy Roman Empress. She received the sobriquet Messalina of Germany,
2 CONC  and was instrumental in creating the Order of the Dragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara was the daughter of Herman II, Count of Celje and Countess Anna of Schaunberg. Barbara's paternal grandparents were Hermann I, Count of Cilli and his wife, Catherine of Bosnia, a possible sister of Elizabeth of Bosnia. Bar
2 CONC bara's maternal grandparents were Henry III of Schaunberg and his wife Ursula of Görz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Barbara and her cousin and adopted sister Anna married ruling Kings whose recently deceased wives were sisters and relatives of the Celje family. Anna married Władysław, King of Poland and Lithuania in 1402 after the death of
2 CONC  Jadwiga of Poland, while Barbara married Sigismund, King of Hungary in 1408 after the death of Mary of Hungary.[1] This marriage was to strengthen Sigismund's grip on the Hungarian throne, as through her father Barbara could trac
2 CONC e her descent not only to the Slovenian rulers of Celje and the Kotromanic of Bosnia to the Nemanjic kings of Serbia and to King Stephen V of Hungary).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigismund, a younger son of Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor later succeeded to the rule in Germany (1410), Bohemia (1419) and was crowned Holy Roman Emperor himself in 1433.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara gave birth to a daughter, Elisabeth, Sigismund's only surviving issue and heiress, who married King Albert II of Germany. Barbara lived to see her three grandchildren, Anne, Elisabeth and Ladislas. She is one of the ancest
2 CONC resses of modern European royal families, her blood flowing in the veins of most of today's dynasties. However, being mother only of a daughter, Barbara's position was weak, but she was nevertheless considered dangerous and evil b
2 CONC y the Hungarian nobility. For the last weeks of her husband's life, Barbara was imprisoned and was not released before his death. She spent the rest of her life as dowager queen in Bohemia, where she was accused of plotting agains
2 CONC t the regime.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara's father Hermann II, as the father-in-law of both feuding Sigismund and Jagiello, played a crucial role in the 1410 pre-Battle of Tannenberg politics by helping prevent Sigismund, who was in alliance with the Teutonic Knig
2 CONC hts, to attack Jagiello. Jagiello with his Slavic allies defeated the Knights who led the combatants provided by 22 western states, including the Pope.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Genetics=
2 CONT Barbara of Celje is a direct matrilineal ancestor of Nicholas II of Russia. Provided the genealogy is correct, this implies that she and all her matrilineal relatives were members of mitochondrial haplogroup Haplogroup T. This inc
2 CONC ludes her many female-line descendants among European nobility. Her great-grandfather was Vladislav Kotromanić, and her great-grandmother was Croatian countess Jelena Šubić, mother of Bosnian King Tvrtko I of Bosnia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ???Her great-grandfather was Stephen II of Bosnia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara's most distantly recorded maternal ancestor is Adelheid von Alpeck (died 1280), daughter of Witegow Von Alpeck.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her great-great-great-great-great granddaughter was Anne of Denmark, the wife of James I of England and mother of Charles I of England, and of Elizabeth Queen of Bohemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara at the council of Constance
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cillei Borbála[2] (1392 – Mělník, Csehország, 1451. július 11.) (németül: Barbara von Cilli; csehül: Barbora Cellská; szlovénül és horvátul: Barbara Celjska) magyar, horvát, német és cseh királyné, német-római császárné, Magyarors
2 CONC zág régense. Luxemburgi Zsigmond második felesége. Cillei Hermann horvát-szlavón bán lánya.
