2 CONT '''Humphrey PLANTAGENET (2º D. Gloucester)'''
2 CONT Born: 3 Oct 1390
2 CONT Acceded: 16 May 1414
2 CONT Died: 23 Feb 1447, Bury St. Edmunds, Suffolk, England
2 CONT Buried: 4 Mar 1447, St. Albans Abbey, Hertfordshire, England
2 CONT Notes: Knight of the Garter. Earl of Pembroke. Regent of England. Founded the Bodleian Library and built the Oxford divinity school. Weir says Eleanor died at Peel Castle, Isle of Man. She was convicted of practising whichcraft up
2 CONC on Henry VI. The Complete Peerage agrees. She may have born Humphrey two children BEF they married, but there are no clear details. The Complete Peerage vol.X,p.397.
2 CONT Father: HENRY IV PLANTAGENET (King of England)
2 CONT Mother: Mary De BOHUN (C. Derby)
2 CONT Married 1: Eleanor COBHAM (b. Sterborough Castle, Kent - d. 1454, Peel Castle, Isle of Man) 1428
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Arthur PLANTAGENET
2 CONT 2. Antigone PLANTAGENET (C. Tankerville)
2 CONT '''Married 2: Jacqueline WITTELSBACH (C. De Hainault & Holland) 1422, Hadleigh, Essex, England'''
