2 TITL Ladislas Posthumous V of Bohemia & Hungary: d. 1457 at Prague.  Page 148
3 CONT Trager's Chronology.
1 NOTE Ladislas V of Hungary was only 17 years old when he died of the plague in 1457.  His Regent, Janos Hunyadi came to power and became king, succeeding Ladislas V.
2 CONT
2 CONT The tragic and short 17-year life of Ladislas Duke of Austria and ruler of Hungary ended in 1457.  He was born after the death of his father, Albert V.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ladislas V, the posthumous son of Albert, succeeded Ladislas I to the throne of Hungary in 1444.  He ruled until 1457.  and was succeeded by Matthias Corvinus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Ladislaus inherited his father Albert V's half of the Austrian Empire in 1440.  He ruled as Duke of Austria until 1457.  End of the Albertine line of Austria.  The Empire then became under the rule of the Leopoldine line, and
2 CONC  his successors were Duke Albert VI and Archduke Frederick V.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ladislas V was crowned King of Hungary in 1453, under the power of George of Podebrad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ladislas V of Hungary was under the Regency of Janos Hunyadi from 1440 to 1452.  In 1457 Ladislas caused the death of Lazlo Hunyadi, and fled Hungary to go to Prague where he died of the plague.
