1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anne of Bohemia and Austria (1432 – 1462) was a Duchess of Luxembourg in her own right, and as consort, Landgravine of Thuringia and of Saxony. She was born into the House of Habsburg, being the eldest daughter of 
2 CONC Albert of Austria, the future Emperor-Elect. She also was a close descendant of the newly extinct House of Luxembourg, her mother being the last Luxembourg heiress, Elisabeth, queen of Bohemia, the sole daughter of Emperor Sigismu
2 CONC nd. Her posthumous brother Ladislaus, Duke of Austria (1440-57) succeeded, very underage, as king of Bohemia and later also as king of Hungary. Anne also had a younger sister, Elisabeth, who was to become later a queen of Poland a
2 CONC nd grand duchess of Lithuania. On June 2, 1446 the young Anne was married to William "the Brave" of Saxony (1425-82), Landgrave of Thuringia, a younger son of Frederick I "the Warlike" of Saxony. In right of Anne, William became D
2 CONC uke of Luxembourg from 1457 when Anne¨s brother Ladislas died childless, up to 1469, though being all the time in dispute with Philip III, Duke of Burgundy, an usurper, over that possession. William concluded that the possession's
2 CONC  keeping was untenable against Burgundian attacks, and retreated to his Thuringian lands - that however took place when Anne was already dead. They had two surviving daughters: Margaret of Thuringia (1449 - 13 July 1501), who marr
2 CONC ied John II, Elector of Brandenburg, and whose direct main heirs have been Electors of Brandenburg, then Kings of Prussia, and then German Emperors. Katharina of Thuringia (1453 – 10 July 1534), who married Duke Henry II of Münste
2 CONC rberg and who has surviving descendants, mainly among Bohemian high nobility.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anne, Duchess of Luxembourg From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT   (Redirected from Anne of Luxembourg)
2 CONT
2 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources. Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. Unverifiable material may be challenged and removed. (January 2009) Anne of Bohemia and Austria (1432 
2 CONC – 1462) was a Duchess of Luxembourg in her own right, and as consort, Landgravine of Thuringia and of Saxony. She was born into the House of Habsburg, being the eldest daughter of Albert of Austria, the future Emperor-Elect. She a
2 CONC lso was a close descendant of the newly extinct House of Luxembourg, her mother being the last Luxembourg heiress, Elisabeth, queen of Bohemia, the sole daughter of Emperor Sigismund. Her posthumous brother Ladislaus, Duke of Aust
2 CONC ria (1440-57) succeeded, very underage, as king of Bohemia and later also as king of Hungary. Anne also had a younger sister, Elisabeth, who was to become later a queen of Poland and grand duchess of Lithuania. On June 2, 1446 the
2 CONC  young Anne was married to William "the Brave" of Saxony (1425-82), Landgrave of Thuringia, a younger son of Frederick I "the Warlike" of Saxony. In right of Anne, William became Duke of Luxembourg from 1457 when Anne¨s brother La
2 CONC dislas died childless, up to 1469, though being all the time in dispute with Philip III, Duke of Burgundy, an usurper, over that possession. William concluded that the possession's keeping was untenable against Burgundian attacks,
2 CONC  and retreated to his Thuringian lands - that however took place when Anne was already dead. They had two surviving daughters: Margaret of Thuringia (1449 - 13 July 1501), who married John II, Elector of Brandenburg, and whose dir
2 CONC ect main heirs have been Electors of Brandenburg, then Kings of Prussia, and then German Emperors. Katharina of Thuringia (1453 – 10 July 1534), who married Duke Henry II of Münsterberg and who has surviving descendants, mainly am
2 CONC ong Bohemian high nobility. [edit]Genetics
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne's mother Elisabeth of Luxembourg is a direct matrilineal ancestor of Nicholas II of Russia. Provided the genealogy is correct, this implies that all her matrilineal relatives are members of mitochondrial haplogroup Haplogroup
2 CONC  T.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Anne von Habsburg ▼1 F, #113897, b. 12 April 1432, d. 14 November 1462 Last Edited=10 Oct 2007 Consanguinity Index=0.28%
2 CONT      Anne von Habsburg was born on 12 April 1432 at Prague, Czech Republic. ▼2  She was the daughter of Albrecht V von Österreich, Holy Roman Emperor and Elisabeth de Luxembourg. ▼1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Wilhelm III Herzog von Sachsen, son of Friedrich I Kurfürst von Sachsen and Catherine von Braunschweig-Lüneburg, on 20 June 1446. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 14 November 1462 at age 30 at Eckartsberga, Germany. ▼2 Children of Anne von Habsburg and Wilhelm III Herzog von Sachsen -1. Margarete von Sachsen+ b. c 1449, d. 13 Jul 1501 -2. Catherine von Sachsen b. c 1453, d. a 24
2 CONC  Oct 1509
2 CONT
