1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir William Tyndal, KB, of Dene and Hockwold, Norfolk, KB 1473, d. c 1488 (Inq.p.m. 13 Henry VII), inherited Worlington Manor 1484 as one of the heirs of Thomas, Lord Scales, being a descendant of Elizabeth (Scales
2 CONC ) Felbrigg, and he was declared heir by inheritance through his great-grandmother Margaret to the Kingdom of Bohemia; he m. Mary, daughter and heir of Sir Osbert Mondeford of Feltwell, Norfolk, Esq., by Elizabeth Berney.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=mwballard&id=I43448
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.generationsgoneby.com/getperson.php?personID=I17336&tree=1
2 CONT
2 CONT William Tyndale, born Abt. 1440 in Hockwold, Norfolk, England; died Abt. 1488. He was the son of  Thomas Tyndale and  Margaret Yelverton. He married Mary Mondeford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Mondeford She was the daughter Osbert Mondeford and Elizabeth Berney.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Tyndale and Mary Mondeford are:
2 CONT
2 CONT   	6754 	i. 	  	John Tyndale, born Abt. 1480 in Hockwold, England; died October 01, 1539; married Amphillis Coningsby.
2 CONT   		ii. 	  	William Tyndale, born Abt. 1485 in Slymbridge, England; died October 06, 1536 in Vilvorde Castle.
2 CONT  	More About William Tyndale:
2 CONT
