1 NOTE As governor of Transylvania (1511-26) he acted with great vigor and 
2 CONT determination in crushing a peasant uprising (1514), for which he won the 
2 CONT support of the nobility. In 1516 he was appointed regent for the young 
2 CONT King Louis II. After Louis was slain fighting the Turks at the Battle of 
2 CONT Mohács (1526), John was accused by some of deliberately failing to reach 
2 CONT him in time with reinforcements. His subsequent election as king of 
2 CONT Hungary embroiled him in a 12-year war with the future Holy Roman emperor 
2 CONT Ferdinand I, who also claimed the throne. Supported by the Ottoman sultan 
2 CONT Suleiman I, the Magnificent, however, John secured much of Hungary by 
2 CONT 1529. Ferdinand finally recognized him as king in 1538 on the 
2 CONT understanding that Ferdinand would decide John's successor. On the birth 
2 CONT of John's son, John II Zápolya, that agreement was set aside.
