1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gy%C3%B6rgy_Z%C3%A1polya
2 CONT
2 CONT Count György (George) Zápolya de Szepes (Croatian: Juraj Zapolja, Hungarian: Szapolyai György or Zápolya György, Romanian: Gheorghe Zápolya, Slovak: Juraj Zápoľský; c. 1488 – 29 August 1526) was a Hungarian magnate, son of Palatin
2 CONC e István Zápolya and younger brother of King John I of Hungary (János Zápolya). He served as Hereditatry Lord Lieutenant (Count; supremus et perpetuus comes) of Szepes County.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was relegated to the political life besides his brother. He was engaged Elisabeth Corvinus, daughter of John Corvinus, in 1504, but the last surviving member of the Hunyadi family died in 1508. He became one of the commanders o
2 CONC f the Hungarian Royal Army in the Battle of Mohács, the other one was Archbishop of Kalocsa Pál Tomori. György Zápolya disappeared and presumably died in the battle.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a hypothesis by a court chaplain, Miklós Tatai, Zápolya murdered King Louis II of Hungary, who escaped from the battle, in the house of the vicar in Dunaszekcső. The historians do not accept this report as credible.
