1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Family tree of the Counts Von Oettingen=
2 CONT We can find Anna under H5. http://genealogy.euweb.cz/oett/oett1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =Oettingen or Öttingen ?=
2 CONT Anna was Countess of Oettingen, a place or city in Bavaria, Germany. The name of the place is Oettingen but was in the past also written with an - ö - instead of - oe -. The German surname LÖWE became LOEWE overseas (Lion in Germa
2 CONC n), because people did not use this letter - ö -.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Öttingen is a place now called Oettingen in Germany=
2 CONT The name Öttingen comes from a place called by the same name, the correct name used now by the Germans themselves is Oettingen, as we can see in the German sites below. The mother of Wilhelm was called in this German wikipedia sit
2 CONC e: Gräfin Anna zu Oettingen. 
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oettingen_in_Bayern
2 CONT * http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_der_%C3%84ltere_von_Waldburg-Trauchburg 
2 CONT
2 CONT =More about the Counts of Oettingen and the place they were Lord of, called Oettingen:=
2 CONT * In Dutch: http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graafschap_Oettingen
2 CONT * In Dutch:  http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graafschap_Oettingen 
2 CONT * In English:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oettingen-Oettingen
2 CONT * In English:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oettingen_in_Bayern
2 CONT * In English:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Oettingen-Wallerstein
2 CONT * In English:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Oettingen-Oettingen
2 CONT * In English:  http://www.oettingen.de/index.php?id=110,9
2 CONT
