1 NOTE     Line 9426 from GEDCOM File not recognizable or too long:
2 CONT     NAME Charles "The Brave" Duke Of /BURGUNDY/
1 NOTE Charles le Tâemâeraire mourant sans postâeritâe mãale, le duchâe de Bourgogne fait retour au roi de France, son suzerain.
1 NOTE Known as Charles the Bold.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "THE BOLD"; DUKE OF BURGUNDY 1467-1477; KILLED IN BATTLE
1 NOTE In 1452 he became count of Charolais. When King Louis XI of France forced 
2 CONT Philip to cede some towns on the Somme River, Charles formed the League of 
2 CONT the Public Weal, an alliance of noblemen. League forces threatened Paris 
2 CONT and defeated the king at Montlhéry, near Paris, in 1465. The result was 
2 CONT the Treaty of Conflans, by which the towns on the Somme were restored and 
2 CONT the counties of Boulogne, Guines, and Ponthieu were granted to Charles. 
2 CONT Succeeding his father as duke in 1467, he became ruler of the territories 
2 CONT that constitute the Low Countries as well as the duchy of Burgundy and 
2 CONT Franche Comté, or the Free County of Burgundy. In 1468, Charles formed an 
2 CONT alliance with his wife's brother, Edward IV, king of England. Richer and 
2 CONT more powerful than any other prince, Charles planned to restore the old 
2 CONT kingdom of Burgundy and fought a series of intermittent wars with France. 
2 CONT In 1475 Charles made himself master of Lorraine. In March of the following 
2 CONT year he invaded Switzerland and was defeated at Grandson. Three months 
2 CONT later he suffered a still more severe defeat at Morat (now Murten). 
2 CONT Nevertheless Charles refused to agree to peace terms and laid siege to 
2 CONT Nancy in October 1476. There he was defeated and killed. His daughter and 
2 CONT heiress, Mary of Burgundy, soon thereafter married Maximilian of Habsburg, 
2 CONT but Maximilian was forced to relinquish all the Burgundian lands except 
2 CONT Flanders.
1 NOTE Helped his wife�s brother to regain the throne (Edward IV). Brother-in-law of Sir Thomas St. Leger. Duke of Burgundy, Holland and Brabant. Count of Flanders, Luxembourg and Namur. [THELMA.GED]
