1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00004544&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Wikipedia:''' [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Thuringia  English ] [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarete_von_Sachsen_(1449%E2%80%931501)_ Deutsch]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wettin-120]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margarete of Saxony, by marriage Electress of Brandenburg, was the daughter of William III "the Brave", Landgrave of Thuringia, and his wife Anna, archduchess of Austria. She was born in Weimar in 1449[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Johann Cicero, Elector of Brandenburg, on 26 August 1476 in Berlin[1]. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter (1480-1482) Wolgang (1482-1482) Joachim Nestor, Elector of Brandenburg Elisabeth, died young (1486) Anna, married Frederik I, King of Denmark Ursula, married Duke Henry V of Mecklenburg Albrecht, Cardinal, Elector of Main
2 CONC z. Margaret died on 13 July 1501 in Spandau near Berlin, and was buried in Berlin[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Cawley, Charles. Medieval Lands: A Prosopography of Medieval European Noble and Royal Families. Saxony Dukes, chap. 7 Electors of Saxony, Wettin Anna. Online at Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Website (acce
2 CONC ssed 2017).
