1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =KATHARINA von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of HEINRICH Herzog von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel & his wife Katharina von Pommern (-Neuhaus 29 Jun 1563, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral). 
2 CONT * House: House of Welf (by birth) House of Ascania (by marriage)
2 CONT * BIRTH: January 01, 1488 in Wolfenbüttel, Braunschweig-Lüneburg, 
2 CONT * Death:	June 19, 1563 (75) in Neuhaus, Lauenburg, Deutschland(HRR)
2 CONT * Catherine was a strict Catholic with close ties to her relative in Brunswick kin. This induced Gustav I of Sweden, to marry her daughter, in an attempt to the Catholic German princes from supporting of King Christian II of Denma
2 CONC rk.[1]
2 CONT * At the marriage of her eldest son, she entered into negotiations with his later mother-in-law Catherine of Mecklenburg, without the knowledge and to the detriment of the Wettin family head John Frederick of Saxony.[2
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#MagnusIdied1543A '''MAGNUS I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg.'''] He converted to Lutheranism in 1531[716] married (Wolfenbüttel [17/20] Nov 1509) KATHARINA von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel, 
2 CONC daughter of HEINRICH Herzog von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel & his wife Katharina von Pommern (-Neuhaus 29 Jun 1563, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).   
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married on 20 November 1509 in Wolfenbüttel Duke Magnus I of Saxe-Lauenburg (1470–1543). Her father summoned the Parliament in 1509 to collect a lady tax, because he found himself unable to pay the dowry alone. Only after long n
2 CONC egotiations, did the Parliament grant three rounds of real estate tax, to generate for money for a dowry and jewels for the princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#MagnusIdied1543A Children of MAGNUS I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg & KATHARINA von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1).         '''FRANZ von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (1510-Buxtehude 19 Mar 1581, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  He succeeded his father in 1543 as FRANZ I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg.  He abdicated in favour of his son in 1571 but resume
2 CONC d power in 1574.  m (Dresden 8 Feb 1540) SIBYLLE von Sachsen, daughter of HEINRICH V "der Fromme" Herzog von Sachsen & his wife Katharina von Mecklenburg (Freiberg 2 May 1515-Buxtehude 18 Jul 1592, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Mistr
2 CONC ess (1): ---.  Mistress (2): ELSE Rautenstein, daughter of HEINRICH Rautenstein, from Otterndorf.  She married (before 13 Nov 1573) Hermann Albrecht, son of --- (1542-1544).  Franz I & his wife had eight children: 
2 CONT * 2).         '''DOROTHEA von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (9 Jul 1511-Sonderburg 7 Oct 1571, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  m (Lauenburg 29 Oct 1525) CHRISTIAN of Denmark, son of FREDERIK I King of Denmark, King of Norway & his first wife Ann
2 CONC a von Brandenburg (Gottorf 12 Aug 1503-Kolding 1 Jan 1559, bur Roskilde Cathedral).  He succeeded in 1533 as Herzog von Schleswig und Holstein, and in 1534 as CHRISTIAN III King of Denmark and Norway. 
2 CONT * 3).        '''KATHARINA von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (24 Sep 1513-Stockholm 23 Sep 1535).  m (Stockholm 24 Sep 1531) as his first wife, '''GUSTAF I King of Sweden,''' son of ERIK Johansson & his wife Cecilia Magnusdotter (Lindholmen
2 CONC  12 May 1496-Stockholm 29 Sep 1560).
2 CONT * 4)         '''SOPHIE von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-Oevelgönne 13 May 1571) m (Oldenburg 1 Jan 1537) ANTON I Graf von Oldenburg und Delmenhorst, son of JOHANN VI Graf von Oldenburg und Delmenhorst & his wife Anna von Anhalt (1505-Ol
2 CONC denburg 22 Jan 1573, bur Oldenburg St Lambert).  
2 CONT * 5)         '''KLARA von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (13 Dec 1518-Barth auf Rügen 27 Mar 1576, bur Barth Marienkirche).  m (Neuhaus im Darssingk 29 Sep 1547) FRANZ Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg in Gifhorn, son of HEINRICH "der Mittle
2 CONC re" Herzog von Braunschweig in Lüneburg & his first wife Margareta von Sachsen (Ulzen 23 Nov 1508-Gifhorn 22/23 Nov 1549, bur Gifhorn).
2 CONT * 6)        '''URSULA''' (-Minden 31 Dec 1577, bur Minden).  m (Schwerin 24 May 1551) as his third wife, HEINRICH V "der Friedfertige" Herzog von Mecklenburg, son of MAGNUS II Herzog von Mecklenburg & his wife Sophie von Pommern-S
2 CONC tettin (3 May 1479-Schwerin 6 Feb 1552, bur Schwerin Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - Project MedLands Saxony 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Royal descendants are all KATHARINA von Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel direct-line descendants=
2 CONT
2 CONT * The current reigning monarchs Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom,
2 CONT * King Carl XVI Gustaf of Sweden, 
2 CONT * King Juan Carlos I of Spain, 
2 CONT * King Harald V of Norway, 
2 CONT * Willem-Alexander of the Netherlands, 
2 CONT * Queen Margrethe II of Denmark, 
2 CONT * King Albert II of Belgium 
2 CONT * Grand Duke Henri of Luxembourg 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catherine_of_Brunswick-Wolfenb%C3%BCttel,_Duchess_of_Saxe-Lauenburg Catherine of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel, Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg]
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel (1488 – 29 June 1563, Neuhaus upon Elbe) was a member of the house of Welf and a Princess of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel and by marriage Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine was a daughter of the Duke Henry IV of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1463–1514) from his marriage to Catherine of Pomerania (1465–1526), daughter of the Duke Erich II of Pomerania.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married on 20 November 1509 in Wolfenbüttel Duke Magnus I of Saxe-Lauenburg (1470–1543). Her father summoned the Parliament in 1509 to collect a lady tax, because he found himself unable to pay the dowry alone. Only after long
2 CONC  negotiations, did the Parliament grant three rounds of real estate tax, to generate for money for a dowry and jewels for the princess.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine was a strict Catholic with close ties to her relative in Brunswick kin. This induced Gustav I of Sweden, to marry her daughter, in an attempt to the Catholic German princes from supporting of King Christian II of Denmark
2 CONC .[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT At the marriage of her eldest son, she entered into negotiations with his later mother-in-law Catherine of Mecklenburg, without the knowledge and to the detriment of the Wettin family head John Frederick of Saxony.[2]
2 CONT
