2 CONT '''Vladislav II, King of Bohemia and Hungary'''1 
2 CONT M, #112022, '''b. 1 March 1456, d. 13 March 1516'''
2 CONT Last Edited=10 Oct 2007
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.05%
2 CONT '''     Vladislav II, King of Bohemia and Hungary was born on 1 March 1456 at Krakow, PolandG.2 He was the son of''' Casimir IV Jagiellon, King of Poland and Elisabeth von Habsburg.3 '''He married, firstly, Beatrix of Naples''', d
2 CONC aughter of Ferdinand I, King of Naples, '''in 1490.4 He and Beatrix of Naples were divorced in 1500.4 He married, secondly, Anne de Foix, Comtesse de Candale''', daughter of Gaston II de Foix, Comte de Candale and Catherine de Foi
2 CONC x, '''on 6 October 1502 at Budapest, HungaryG.2 He died on 13 March 1516 at age 60 at Budapest, Hungary'''G.2
2 CONT '''     He was a member of the House of Jagellon. He succeeded as the King Vladislav II of Bohemia in 1471.4 He gained the title of King Wladislas II of Hungary in 1490.'''4
2 CONT '''Children of Vladislav II, King of Bohemia and Hungary and Anne de Foix, Comtesse de Candale'''
2 CONT 1. Anna Jagellon+1 b. 23 Jul 1503, d. 27 Jan 1547
2 CONT 2. Lajos II, King of Bohemia and Hungary1 b. 1506, d. 1526
