1 NOTE He wa called The Old.  Also grand duke of Lithuania (1506-48). Sigismund 
2 CONT succeeded his brother Alexander. He opposed the rising power of the 
2 CONT gentry, allying himself instead with the higher nobles, or magnates, to 
2 CONT whom he gave greater authority over the peasantry. Early in his reign he 
2 CONT fought a series of indecisive wars with Basil III of Muscovy (1479-1533). 
2 CONT By the Treaty of Vienna (1515) he renounced his claim to the Hungarian 
2 CONT throne in favor of the Austrian Habsburgs, who in return surrendered their 
2 CONT claim to Poland. From 1519 to 1521 he was at war with his nephew, Albert 
2 CONT of Hohenzollern (1490-1568), grand master of the Teutonic Knights, and 
2 CONT Albert eventually recognized (1525) him as his overlord. A patron of the 
2 CONT arts, Sigismund embellished the cathedral and royal palace of Kraków in 
2 CONT the Italian Renaissance style.
1 NOTE KING OF POLAND 1506-1548 AS SIGISMUND I
