1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Juan II .. m secondly (Madrigalejo [15] Aug 1447) Infanta dona ISABEL de Portugal, daughter of Infante dom JOÃO de Portugal Duque de Beja & his wife dona Isabel de Bragança ([1428]-Arevalo 15 Aug 1496, bur Car
2 CONC thusian convent at Miraflora near Burgos).  When her husband died, she retired with her two children to the fortress of Arevalo, where she gradually went insane. 
2 CONT >1. '''Infanta doña ISABEL de Castilla y León (Madrigal de las Altas Torres 22 Apr 1451-Castillo de la Mota, Medina del Campo 26 Nov 1504).'''  Her mother took her to the fortress of Arevalo when her father died, but her half-brot
2 CONC her Enrique IV recalled her and her brother to court in 1462.  Betrothed to Pr de Viana, she was also promised to Alfonso V King of Portugal, and to Girón, brother of Villena following the latter's machinations.  She succeeded her
2 CONC  half-brother in 1474 as ISABEL I Queen of Castile and León, insisting on governing Castile in her own not her husband's name.  She and husband successfully outmanoeuvred Portugal's plans to place Juana la Beltraneja on the throne
2 CONC .  Her achievements as Queen included reform of the privileges of the nobility, the cause of such difficulties for her two predecessors, and renovation of the legal system.  With the aim of achieving religious unification, she int
2 CONC roduced the Inquisition 11 Aug 1480.  The reconquest of the final territories held by the Moors lasted 10 years, marked by defeats at Loja and Axarquia, but culminating in the capitulation of Granada 2 Jan 1492.  The expulsion of 
2 CONC the Jews followed, with disastrous economic consequences for the country.  Isabel and her husband sponsored the voyage of Cristóbal Colon, resulting in the discovery of America which signalled the start of Spain's imperial expansi
2 CONC on.  m (Valladolid 19 Oct 1469) as his first wife, Infante don FERNANDO de Aragón, son of JUAN II King of Aragon and Navarre & his second wife Juana Enríquez Señora de Casarrubios del Monte y Arroyojolinos (Soa 10 Mar 1452-Madrigu
2 CONC alejo 25 Jan 1516).  He succeeded in 1479 as FERNANDO II King of Aragon, Sicily, Naples and Mallorca. https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CASTILE.htm#JuanIIdied1454B]]
2 CONT >King Fernando II & his first wife [ISABEL I Queen of Castile] had six children:
2 CONT >>1.         Infanta doña ISABEL de Castilla y Aragón (Duenas 2 Oct 1470-Zaragoza 23 Aug 1498, bur Toledo).  
2 CONT >>2.         Infante don JUAN de Castilla y Aragón (Seville 30 Jun 1478-Salamanca 4 Oct 1497, bur Álava).  Principe de Asturias.  
2 CONT >>3.         Infanta doña JUANA de Castilla y Aragón (Toledo 6 Nov 1479-Tordesillas 11 Apr 1555). 
2 CONT >>4.         Infanta doña MARÍA de Castilla y Aragón (Córdoba 29 Jun 1482-Lisbon 7 Mar 1517, bur Belem, Monastery of São Geronimo).  
2 CONT >>5.         daughter stillborn (Córdoba 30 Jun 1482).  Twin with María. 
2 CONT >>6.         Infanta doña CATALINA de Castilla y Aragón (Alcalá de Henares 16 Dec 1485-Kimbolton Castle, Huntingdonshire 7 Jan 1536, bur Peterborough Cathedral).  https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARAGON%20&%20CATALONIA.htm#Fernand
2 CONC oIIdied1516B
