1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catherine,_Princess_of_Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Catherine
2 CONT Princess of Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT Born	5 October 1422
2 CONT Illescas, Toledo
2 CONT Died	17 September 1424
2 CONT (age 1 year, 348 days)
2 CONT Madrigal de las Altas Torres
2 CONT Burial	Miraflores Monastery, Burgos
2 CONT House	Trastámara
2 CONT Father	John II of Castile
2 CONT Mother	Maria of Aragon
2 CONT Religion	Roman Catholicism
2 CONT Catherine of Castile (Castilian: Catalina de Castilla; 5 October 1422 - 17 September 1424) was suo jure Princess of Asturias and heiress presumptive to the Castilian throne all her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine was born on 5 October 1422 in Illescas, Toledo. She was the first child of King John II of Castile and his first wife, Maria of Aragon. Named after her aunt and grandmother, the Duchess of Villena and Catherine of Lancas
2 CONC ter, she immediately became heiress presumptive to the throne of Castile upon her birth. The Infanta was formally recognised as successor to the throne of the kingdom and sworn in as Princess of Asturias on 1 January 1423 by the C
2 CONC ortes of Toledo.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the Princess of Asturias did not live long enough to succeed her father as Queen of Castile. She died in Madrigal de las Altas Torres on 17 September 1424. Her younger sister, Infanta Eleanor, replaced her as heiress and 
2 CONC Princess of Asturias. Princess Catherine is buried in Miraflores Charterhouse, along with her father and stepmother, Isabella of Portugal.[2]
