2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon (Spanish: Leonor) (1425-Tudela, 1479), Regent (1455-1479) and the queen regnant (1479) of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the third and youngest daughter of John II of Aragón and queen Blanche I of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born February 2, 1425, and was acclaimed by the cortes in Pamplona, August 9, 1427, being the legitimate heir of Charles, Prince of Viana, and Blanche.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Gaston IV, count of Foix, and had the following children with him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaston (1444-1470), he married Princess Magdalena of Valois of France in 1462 and their children Francis and Catherine both succeeded to Navarre in turn upon the death of their grandmother Eleanor, married Marie d'Orléans
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1450-1500), viscount of Narbonne, whose daughter Germaine of Foix was second wife to Ferdinand II of Aragon,
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter (1449-1490), cardinal and bishop of Arles
2 CONT
2 CONT James (1455-1500), count of Cortes, married Catherine of Beaumont
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (1452-1497), married William VIII, marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (1454-1476), married John V, count of Armagnac
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Foix (1453-1486), married Francis II, duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (b.1455), married Gaston II de Foix, Count of Candale and Benauges
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella b.1462, married Guy of Pons
2 CONT
2 CONT Leonor
2 CONT
2 CONT Ana
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Wiki: Eleanor of Navarre
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Aragon (Spanish: Leonor) (Olite, Navarre (now Spain), 2 February 1426 - Tudela, Navarre (now Spain), 12 February 1479), Regent (1455-1479) and the queen regnant of Navarre in 1479. She was crowned on 28 January 1479 in 
2 CONC Tudela.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Life
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the third and youngest daughter of John II of Aragón and queen Blanche I of Navarre. She was born February 2, 1426, and was acclaimed by the cortes in Pamplona, August 9, 1427, as the legitimate heir of Charles, Prince of 
2 CONC Viana, and Blanche.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Gaston IV, count of Foix, and had the following children with him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaston (1444-1470), he married Princess Magdalena of Valois of France in 1462 and their children Francis and Catherine both succeeded to Navarre in turn upon the death of their grandmother Eleanor, married Marie d'Orléans
2 CONT
