1 TITL Infante
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Infante Fernando of Portugal, Prince of Portugal, Duke of Viseu (1433–1470, English: Ferdinand, pron. IPA [f??'n??du]) was the third son of Portuguese King Edward of Portugal and his wife Leonor of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand was born in Almeirim on November 17, 1433. He became Duke of Viseu when his uncle Henry the Navigator died in 1460. He also succeeded his uncle as Master of the Order of Aviz and responsible for the Discoveries (1460-147
2 CONC 0).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was twice Prince of Portugal (title attributed to the presunptive heir to the throne) first between 1438 and 1451, because his brother Edward had no children. In 1451 Prince João was born, but died months later. Fernando was th
2 CONC en given the title of Prince of Portugal for a second time until the next year, when Edward's first daughter Princess Joana was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his cousin Beatrice of Portugal (Portuguese: Beatriz) in 1447, daughter of Infante João, Lord of Reguengos (his uncle).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Fernando, Duke of Viseu
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT The Infante Fernando, Prince of Portugal, Duke of Viseu (1433–1470, English: Ferdinand, pronounced [fɨɾˈnɐ̃du]) was the third son of Portuguese King Edward of Portugal and his wife Leonor of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand was born in Almeirim on November 17, 1433. He became Duke of Viseu when his uncle Henry the Navigator died in 1460. He also succeeded his uncle as Master of the Order of Aviz and responsible for the Discoveries (1460-147
2 CONC 0).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was twice Prince of Portugal (title attributed to the presumptive heir to the throne) first between 1438 and 1451, because his brother Edward had no children. In 1451 Prince João was born, but died months later. Fernando was th
2 CONC en given the title of Prince of Portugal for a second time until the next year, when Edward's first daughter Princess Joana was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his cousin Beatrice of Portugal (Portuguese: Beatriz) in 1447, daughter of Infante João, Lord of Reguengos (his uncle).
2 CONT
2 CONT From that marriage Ferdinand had nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante João of Viseu (1448-1472), 3rd Duke of Viseu, 2nd Duke of Beja, 6th general of the kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Diogo of Viseu (1450-1484), 4th Duke of Viseu, 3rd Duke of Beja.
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Duarte of Viseu
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Dinis of Viseu
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Simão of Viseu
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Leonor of Viseu (1458-1525), married John II of Portugal and became Queen of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Isabel of Viseu (1459-1521), married Ferdinand II, Duke of Braganza,
2 CONT
2 CONT Infante Manuel of Viseu, king of Portugal as Manuel I after the death of his cousin John II of Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Infanta Catarina of Viseu
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infante_Fernando,_Duke_of_Viseu
