1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_of_Baden
2 CONT
2 CONT Albert was married twice. First, he married 12 November 1446 Margarete of Baden, daughter of Markgrave Jakob I of Baden and Catherine of Lorraine. From this marriage he had following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Wolfgang, born and died in 1450.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cicero, Elector of Brandenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich, died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ursula (25 September 1450–25 October 1508, Breslau), married Duke Heinrich I of Münsterberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth, (29 October 1451, Ansbach–28 March 1524, Nürtingen), married Eberhard II, Duke of Württemberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margareta (18 April 1453–27 April 1509), Abbess of St.Klara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob, Margrave of Baden-Baden
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 25 July 1422 Catherine of Lorraine, daughter of Charles II, Duke of Lorraine and Margaret of the Palatinate. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles I, Margrave of Baden-Baden (d. 24 February 1475, Pforzheim).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard II, Margrave of Baden-Baden (later beatified) (1428–12 July 1458, Moncalieri).
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann (1430–9 February 1503, Ehrenbreitstein), Archbishop of Trier.
2 CONT
2 CONT George (1433–11 February 1484, Moyen), Bishop of Metz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Markus (1434–1 September 1478), abbot in Liège.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margarete (1431–24 October 1457, Ansbach), married 1446 to Albert III, Margrave of Brandenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilde (d. 1485), Abbess of Trier.
