2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf of Egmond
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf of Egmond (Grave, January 12, 1438 - Tournai, June 27, 1477) was a Duke of Guelders from 1465–1471 and in 1477.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Arnold of Egmond, Duke of Guelders and Catherine of Cleves, daughter of Adolph I, Duke of Cleves.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the battle of succession for Guelders, he imprisoned in 1465 his own father and became Duke with the support of Philip the Good, who also made him Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece. In 1468 he won the Battle of Straelen 
2 CONC against Cleves, but Charles the Bold reinstated his father Arnold, and Adolf was imprisoned in Hesdin.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Charles the Bold in 1477, he was liberated by the Flemish.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died the same year at the head of a Flemish army besieging Tournai, after the States of Guelders had recognized him as Duke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf married Catharine of Bourbon (1440–1469), daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon, in 1463. They had 2 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Philippa (1467–1547), married in 1485 René II, Duke of Lorraine (1451–1508)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Charles (1467–1538), later Duke of Guelders, married in 1518 with Elisabeth of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1494–1572), daughter of Henry I of Lüneburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnold 	Duke of Guelders
2 CONT
2 CONT 1465–1471 	Succeeded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnold
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles the Bold 	Duke of Guelders
2 CONT
2 CONT 1477–1477 	Succeeded by
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT This page was last modified on 27 April 2010 at 04:26.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Adolf of Egmond (Grave, January 12, 1438 - Tournai, June 27, 1477) was a Duke of Guelders, Count of Zutphen from 1465–1471 and in 1477.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Arnold, Duke of Guelders and Catherine of Cleves, daughter of Adolph I, Duke of Cleves.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the battle of succession for Guelders, he imprisoned in 1465 his own father and became Duke with the support of Philip the Good, who also made him Knight in the Order of the Golden Fleece. In 1468 he won the Battle of Straelen 
2 CONC against Cleves, but Charles the Bold reinstated his father Arnold, and Adolf was imprisoned in Hesdin.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Charles the Bold in 1477, he was liberated by the Flemish.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died the same year at the head of a Flemish army besieging Tournai, after the States of Guelders had recognized him as Duke.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adolf married Catharine of Bourbon (1440–1469), daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon, in 1463. They had 2 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa (1467–1547), married in 1485 René II, Duke of Lorraine (1451–1508)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles (1467–1538), later Duke of Guelders, married in 1518 with Elisabeth of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1494–1572), daughter of Henry I of Lüneburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://thepeerage.com/p477.htm#i4763 The Peerage]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Stamboom nr. :  104.596.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generatie :  17.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hij is geboren in Doornik - Tournai is de franse vertaling van Doornik.
