1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =John II, Duke of Cleves=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Johann II. (Born 13 April 1458– 15 March 1521) was the Duke of Cleves and count of Mark from 1481 to 1521.
2 CONT * John II, "The Babymaker", Duke of Cleves, Count of Mark, (German: Johann II. "der Kindermacher", Herzog von Kleve, Graf von Mark) (13 April 1458 – 15 March 1521) was a son of John I, Duke of Cleves and Elizabeth of Nevers.[1] He
2 CONC  ruled Cleves from 1481 to his death in 1521. He was called "The Babymaker" since he fathered sixty-three illegitimate children [2] before his marriage with Mathilde of Hesse in 1489. She was the daughter of Henry III, Landgrave o
2 CONC f Upper Hesse and his wife Anna of Katzenelnbogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FRANCONIA%20(LOWER%20RHINE).htm#JohannKlevedied1521 Project MedLands, FRANCONIA]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHANN von Kleve, son of ADOLF Duke of Kleve & his second wife Marie de Bourgogne [Valois-Capet] (Kleve 16 Feb 1419-5 Sep 1481).'''  Wernher Teschenmacher’s Annales Cliviæ (1630s) records the birth “die S. Julianæ” 1419 of “Joa
2 CONC nnes, patris successor”, but the editor of the edition consulted quotes no earlier primary source which confirms this information[1511].  Duke of Kleve.  '''married  (contract Bruges 25 Mar 1455, Bruges 22 Apr 1455) ELISABETH de N
2 CONC evers, daughter of JEAN de Nevers [later Comte de Nevers] [Bourgogne-Valois] & his first wife Jacqueline d’Ailly ([1439]-21 Jun 1483).'''  The marriage contract between “Jean duc de Clèves et comte de la Mark” and “Elisabeth de Bo
2 CONC urgogne, fille de Jean de Bourgogne comte d’Estampes et sgr de Dourdan, et de Jacqueline d’Ailly sa femme” is dated 25 Mar 1455[1512].  Heiress of Nevers and Eu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann & his wife ELISABETH de Nevers had six children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''JOHANN von Kleve "der Kindermacher"''' (Kleve 14 Apr 1458-15 Jan 1521, bur Kleve Stiftskirche).  Duke of Kleve.  '''married (Soest 3 Nov 1489) MATHILDE von Hessen, daughter of HEINRICH III Landgraf zu Hessen, Graf 
2 CONC zu Ziegenhain und Nidda, Herr von Oberhessen & his wife Anna von Katzenelnbogen (Blankenstein Jul 1473-Köln 19 Feb 1505, bur Kleve Stiftskirche).'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann & his wife MATHILDE von Hessen had three children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* a)         '''JOHANN von Kleve''' (Kleve 10 Nov 1490-6 Feb 1539, bur Kleve).  Duke of Jülich and Berg 1511.  Duke of Kleve 1521.  Duke of Jülich-Kleve-Berg 1524. 
2 CONT >>>>>* b)         '''ANNA''' (Kleve 21 May 1495-24 May 1567).  '''married  (1518) PHILIPP Graf von Waldeck-Eisenberg, son of --- (1486-1539).''' 
2 CONT >>>>>*c)         '''ADOLF''' (Kleve 23 Jan 1498-Spain 1525). 
2 CONT * 2.         '''ADOLF''' (Kleve 28 Apr 1461-5 Apr 1498).  Priest at Liège. 
2 CONT * 3.         '''ENGELBERT''' (Kleve 26 Sep 1462-21 Nov 1506, bur Nevers Franciscan Church).  Comte de Nevers. 
2 CONT * 4.         '''DIETRICH''' (Kleve 29 Jun 1464-). 
2 CONT * 5.         '''MARIE''' (Kleve 16 Aug 1465-7 Oct 1513, bur Kleve). 
2 CONT * 6.         '''PHILIPP''' (Kleve 1 Jan 1467-Nevers 5 Mar 1505).  Bishop of Nevers 1500, Bishop of Amiens 1501.  Bishop of Autun 1503. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II,_Duke_of_Cleves John II, Duke of Cleves, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT John II, "The Babymaker", Duke of Cleves, Count of Mark, (German: Johann II. "der Kindermacher", Herzog von Kleve, Graf von Mark) (13 April 1458 – 15 March 1521) was a son of John I, Duke of Cleves and Elizabeth of Nevers.[1] He r
2 CONC uled Cleves from 1481 to his death in 1521. He was called "The Babymaker" as he had fathered sixty-three illegitimate children[2] prior to his marriage with Mathilde of Hesse in 1489.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pope Innocent VIII awarded John the Golden Rose on 15 April 1489. This is remarkable in light of the fact that John, with his alleged 63 illegitimate children, had the dubious reputation of being a "child maker". From then on, Joh
2 CONC n called himself "Johann von Kleve, Count of La Marck and Katzenelnbogen".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage and issue'''
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Matilda of Hesse,[3] daughter of Henry III, Landgrave of Upper Hesse and Anna of Katzenelnbogen,[4] on 3 November 1489 in Soest. They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John''' (1490–1539), succeeded as Duke of Cleves and Count of the Marck[5]
2 CONT * '''Anna''' (1495–1567), married in 1518 with count Philip III of Waldeck-Eisenberg[5]
2 CONT * '''Adolf''' (1498–1525), appointed by his father's cousin Philip of Cleves, Lord of Ravenstein and Wijnendale, as his successor, but died before Philip did in 1528
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Catherine de Chaumont:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Hermann of Cleves seigneur d'Afnois, d'Amazy and Saligny''' (1458-1532), married Leonarde Perreau,[6] legitimized in 1506.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT =With unknown mothers:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Helena (or Hedwig) of Cleves''' (1480-?), married Otto van Büren
2 CONT * '''Joos (Judocus) of Cleves''' (1485-1541)
2 CONT * '''Wilhelm of Cleves''' (c. 1495 -?)
2 CONT * '''Marten of Cleves'''
2 CONT * '''Hendrik of Cleves'''
2 CONT * '''Katharina of Cleves''',[7] married Johann von Asschebroick[7] and secondly Johann von Loe
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth of Cleves,''' married Gobert van Bemmel
2 CONT * '''Dietrich of Cleves''' (?-1493)
2 CONT * '''Johann of Cleves'''
2 CONT * '''Adolf of Cleves,''' married Agnes von Hessen zu Hulhausen
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.archive.nrw.de/en/archivsuche '''Source: State Archives of North Rhine-Westphalia, Rhineland Department AA 0058 / Kleve-Marc, Acten AA 0058, Nr. 22, 22) Provision for the illegitimate children of Duke John II of Cleve
2 CONC s-Mark'''.]
2 CONT
