2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa's mother's tombstone
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa was the twin sister of Charles, Duke of Guelders, they were their parents' only children. Her mother was the daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon, and his wife, Agnes of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa's paternal grandparents were Arnold, Duke of Gelderland, and Catherine of Cleves. Catherine was the daughter of Adolph I, Duke of Cleves, and his second wife, Marie of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her aunt was Mary of Guelders, queen and regent of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Life
2 CONT
2 CONT To strengthen the ties between the Kingdom of France and the Duchy of Lorraine, Philippa was chosen as the bride of René II, Duke of Lorraine (1451–1508). The marriage took place in Orléans on 1 September 1485.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her husband Philippa tried to assume the regency of the duchy in the name of her son Antonio, who was only 9 years old, but it was decided that the child was old enough to reign alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 June 1509 she redeemed the lordship of Mayenne from Margaret of Vaudémont, Duchess of Alençon. She retired to the convent Clarisse to Pont-à-Mousson on 15 December 1519 where she remained until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT While at the convent she commanded a magnificent altarpiece for the congregation, it remained there until his death. Her twin brother Charles, Duke of Gelderland, died on 30 June 1538, without legitimate offspring. Philippa claime
2 CONC d the duchies of Gelderland and Jülich but Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor, seized the duchies. She sent the claim to the two duchies to her son Anthony, who added it to his Coat of Arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa died at the convent on 28 February 1547, she was seventy nine years old. She outlived nine of her eleven children and was alive at the time of birth of some great-grandchildren, see lived to see the birth of her grandson 
2 CONC Francis I, Duke of Lorraine's children and her great-granddaughter, Mary, Queen of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa and René had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Charles (b. 17 August 1486, Nancy), d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Francis (5 July 1487, Pont-à-Mousson) (died shortly after birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Antoine, Duke of Lorraine (1489–1544)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Nicholas (9 April 1493, Nancy), d. young
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Claude, Duke of Guise (1496–1550), first Duke of Guise
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John, Cardinal of Lorraine and Bishop of Metz (1498–1550)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Louis, Count of Vaudémont (1500–1528)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Francis, Count of Lambesc (1506–1525)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne (19 December 1490, Bar-le-Duc – 1491)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Isabelle (2 November 1494, Lunéville – bef. 1508)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Claude and Catherine (twins) (24 November 1502, Bar-le-Duc), d. young
