1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Dutch Wikipedia page on Elisabeth von Hessen-Marburg:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisabeth_van_Hessen
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth, Landgravin van Hessen-Marburg (Marburg, mei 1466 - Keulen, 7 of 17 januari 1523) was een dochter van Hendrik van Hessen-Marburg (de Rijke) en Anna van Katzenelnbogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth trouwde op 11 februari 1482 met Jan V van Nassau. Uit dit huwelijk zijn zes kinderen geboren:
2 CONT *1. Hendrik III van Nassau
2 CONT *2. Jan (1484-1504)
2 CONT *3. Ernst (1486)
2 CONT *4. Willem de Rijke
2 CONT *5. Elisabeth van Nassau
2 CONT *6. Maria van Nassau
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth ligt begraven in Siegen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Elisabeth von Hessen:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p11319.htm#i113182
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth von Hessen [1] F, #113182, 
2 CONT *b. 1466, 
2 CONT *d. 1523
2 CONT *Last Edited=28 Jul 2002
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth von Hessen was born in 1466.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Johann V Graf von Nassau-Vianden-Dietz, son of Johann IV Graf von Nassau-Dietz, in 1482.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1523.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Heinrich III Landgraf von Hessen.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elisabeth von Hessen and Johann V Graf von Nassau-Vianden-Dietz
2 CONT *1. Heinrich III Graf von Nassau-Breda+[1] b. 1483, d. 1538
2 CONT *2. Johann von Nassau-Vianden-Dietz [1] b. 1484, d. 1504
2 CONT *3. Wilhelm Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg+[1] b. 10 Apr 1487, d. 6 Oct 1559
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 34. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Women in Power 1500-1540:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.guide2womenleaders.com/womeninpower/Womeninpower1500.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1500-23 Hereditary Countess Elisabeth von Hessen-Marburg of Katzenelnbogen and ¼ of the County of Diez (Germany)
2 CONT
2 CONT After her mother, Anna von Katzenelnbogen, died in 1494 the County was disputed among her and her sister, Duchess Mathilda of Jülich-Berg (d. 1505), and a compromise was not reached until 1520. Elisabeth was married to Johann V Co
2 CONC unt of Nassau, Vianden, Katzenelnbogen and Diez, Baron of Breda, Stadholder of Gelre and Zutphen 1504-1505. She lived (1466-1523).
