1 NOTE !A Thomas Hubbard was burned at the stake on May 5, 1555 in Essex County, England for refusing to recant his Protestantism.
2 CONT !Baptism and Endowment per Temple Submission Record 325-21938.
1 NOTE Children of Thomas Hobart and Audria/Audrey Hara are:
2 CONT
2 CONT    i.   Sir Henry Hobart, born 1563 in Plumstead, Norfolk; died December 29, 1625 in Norfolk; married Dorothy Bell April 21, 1590 in Blickling, Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT    ii.   Sir Miles Hobart, born 1564 in Plumstead, Norfolk; married Margaret Woodhouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT    iii.   Mary Hobart, born 1566 in Plumstead, Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT    iv.   Ellen Hobart, born 1568 in Plumstead, Norfolk; married Daniel Blennerhassett February 12, 1577/78 in Plumstead, Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT    v.   Edmund Hobart, born January 1, 1572/73 in Hingham, co. Norfolk, England; died March 8, 1645/46 in Hingham, Sulfolk, MA; married (1) Margaret Dewey September 7, 1600 in Hingham, Norfolk, England; married (2) Sarah Oakley Oc
2 CONC tober 10, 1634 in Charlestown, Charlestown Co., MA.
1 NOTE Thomas Hubbard is listed in Fox's "Book of Martyrs" as being burned at the stake on May 26, 1555, in Essex, England, for refusing to recant his protestantism.
