2 CONT '''Marguerite de Lorraine '''
2 CONT F, #3213, '''b. 1463, d. 1 November 1521'''
2 CONT Last Edited=10 May 2003
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=2.42%
2 CONT '''     Marguerite de Lorraine was born in 1463. She was the daughter of''' Frederic VI de Vaudémont, Comte de Vaudémont and Yolande d'Anjou. '''She married René d'Alençon, Duc d'Alençon''', son of Jean II d'Alençon, Duc d'Alençon
2 CONC , '''in 1488. She died on 1 November 1521.'''
2 CONT '''Child of Marguerite de Lorraine and René d'Alençon, Duc d'Alençon'''
2 CONT 1. Françoise d'Alençon+ b. bt 1490 - 1491, d. 14 Sep 1550
2 CONT From: https://www.thepeerage.com/p322.htm#i3213
2 CONT _______
2 CONT '''René of Alençon''' (1454 – 1 November 1492) was a French nobleman. He succeeded his father John II of Alençon as Duke of Alençon.
2 CONT Life
2 CONT '''René''' was born in 1454 to the House of Valois-Alençon. He was the son of John II of Alençon and Marie of Armagnac.[1]
2 CONT In 1478, he was restored as Duke of Alençon and Count of Perche, titles which had been confiscated from his family after his father's conviction in 1474.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT His first wife was Marguerite, daughter of William of Harcourt, Count of Tancarville.
2 CONT '''He married a second time on 14 May 1488 at Toul, to Margaret of Lorraine (1463 – 1 November 1521),'''[2] daughter of Frederick, Count of Vaudémont and Yolande of Anjou. '''Margaret bore him three children:'''
2 CONT 1. Charles IV of Alençon (1489–1525)[1]
2 CONT 2. Françoise of Alençon (c. 1490 – 14 September 1550, La Fleche), Duchess of Beaumont, married 1505 in Blois, François, Duke of Longueville (d. 1512),[1] married 1513 Charles, Duke of Vendôme
2 CONT 3. Anne (30 October 1492 – 18 October 1562, Casale Monferrato), Lady of la Guerche, married 31 August 1508 in Blois William IX Paleologos, Marquess of Montferrat[1]
2 CONT He also had several illegitimate children:
2 CONT 1. Charles (d. 1545), Lord of Cany[1]
2 CONT 2. Marguerite, married 1485 Jacques de Boisguyon,[1] married Henri de Bournel
2 CONT 3. Jacqueline, married Gilles des Ormes[1]
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ren%C3%A9,_Duke_of_Alen%C3%A7on
2 CONT __________
