1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00275001&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father's problems with consummating his two marriages was one reason why her paternity was in doubt. Also, both her father and mother were suspected of being the lovers of a handsome young courtier, Don Beltran de la Cueva, wh
2 CONC o, as a result, was reputed to be her father and she became known as 'La Beltraneja'. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Enrique IV tried to have her accepted as his heir and, when that failed, engaged her to his half-brother, Alfonso, who died shortly afterwards, suspected of poisoning. Her next prospective husband was her mother's brother, Al
2 CONC fonso V, King of Portugal, but this marriage also did not take place. In 1530 she died in a convent in Lisbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juana_la_Beltraneja
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana de Trastámara, apodada la Beltraneja (Madrid, marzo de 1462 – Lisboa, 1530). Infanta castellana, reina destronada de Castilla y León, reina consorte de Portugal destituida de su rango, hubo de renunciar por tratado a todos s
2 CONC us títulos y señoríos, incluso a su calidad de infanta castellana y de Alteza, quedando llamada oficialmente, por real decreto portugués, "a Excelente Senhora" (la Excelente Señora), hasta el final de su larga vida en el exilio de
2 CONC  Portugal. Hija legítima y heredera de Enrique IV y de su segunda esposa la reina Juana de Portugal, hija de Eduardo I de Portugal, parte de la nobleza castellana no la aceptaba como hija biológica del rey su padre, a quién acusó 
2 CONC de obligar la reina su mujer a tener un hijo con su favorito, Beltrán de la Cueva, primer duque de Albuquerque, a pesar de que ambos habían jurado solemnemente que no había sido así.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tabla de contenidos
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Infancia 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Esponsales con el duque de Guyena 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Juana e Isabel, sobrina y tía 
2 CONT
