1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Alonso d'Aragona''' (1460–1510), designated heir to Queen Charlotte of Cyprus, who was either married or engaged to Charla of Lusignan (1468 – in prison in Padua, 1480), a natural daughter of Charlotte's half br
2 CONC other, King James II of Cyprus. His young bride was captured by the queen's opponents and died in captivity shortly before her twelfth birthday.[113] After her death, a marriage was proposed between him and Catherine Conaro, but t
2 CONC he plan came to nothing due to the interference of the Republic of Venice. Instead, Charlotte ceded her claims to the Cypriotic throne to her cousin, Charles I of Savoy, in 1485.[114] Alonso was made bishop of Chieti on 28 Februar
2 CONC y 1488 and kept this office until 16 November 1496.
2 CONT
2 CONT #https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_I_of_Naples#Marriages_and_children
