0 @N6000000002188376371@ NOTE Henry III of Castile
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry III (October 4, 1379–1406), sometimes known as Henry the Sufferer or Henry the Infirm (Spanish: Enrique el Doliente) was the son of John I and Eleanor of Aragon, and succeeded him as King of Castile and León in 1390.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry was born in Burgos, the capital of Castile. Before becoming king, he was known by the title Prince of Asturias, designating him as the heir apparent. After succeeding to the throne at 11, Henry took power at 14. He was able 
1 CONC to pacify the nobility and restore royal power. During his reign, the Castilian fleet won several victories against the English; Henry sent a naval fleet in 1400 that destroyed Tétouan in North Africa, a pirate base. In 1402, Henr
1 CONC y began the colonization of the Canary Islands, sending French explorer Jean de Béthencourt. He also sent envoys to Timur.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1388, Henry married Katherine of Lancaster (Catalina de Lancaster; 1372–1418), the daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster and Gaunt's second wife, Constance of Castile, who was the elder daughter of Pedro of Castile. 
1 CONC This ended a dynastic conflict and solidified the House of Trastamara. Henry and Catherine's son became John II of Castile, who succeeded Henry when he died in Toledo, Catherine acting as Regent of Castile because John II was then
1 CONC  underage.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Ancestry
1 CONT Henry's ancestors in three generations Henry III of Castile Father:
1 CONT John I of Castile Paternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Henry II of Castile Paternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Alfonso XI of Castile
1 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Eleanor of Guzman
1 CONT Paternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Juana Manuel of Castile Paternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Juan Manuel, Duke of Peñafiel
1 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Blanca de La Cerda y Lara
1 CONT Mother:
1 CONT Eleanor of Aragon Maternal Grandfather:
1 CONT Peter IV of Aragon Maternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Alfonso IV of Aragon
1 CONT Maternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Teresa d'Entença
1 CONT Maternal Grandmother:
1 CONT Eleanor of Sicily Maternal Great-grandfather:
1 CONT Peter II of Sicily
1 CONT Maternal Great-grandmother:
1 CONT Elisabeth of Carinthia
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Children
1 CONT
1 CONT All of them by his wife Catherine of Lancaster:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Catalina (1402-?)
1 CONT     * John II of Castile
1 CONT     * Maria of Castile. Married Alfonso V of Aragon.
1 CONT
