0 @N6000000002322303469@ NOTE The true founder of the Burgundian state that rivaled France in the 15th
1 CONT century. When he became duke in 1419, his first aim was to extricate himself
1 CONT as expeditiously as possible from the French affair in which his father, Duke
1 CONT John, had been emboiled and that led to his assassination. Behind a facade of
1 CONT courtly splendour, Philip was an aggressive opportunist concentrating on the
1 CONT task of attacking and swallowing up his smaller neighbors, with the duchy of
1 CONT Luxembourg a prize possession (1443).
