1 CONT was archduke Albert V of Austria from infancy in 1404. Apparently, he was the
1 CONT Holy Roman Emperor after his father-in-law, Sigismund, died in 1438. Calling
1 CONT a Diet at Nurnberg in 1438, he ended all feuds based on the right  of private
1 CONT warfare and appointed arbitrators to settle disputes. Though his short rule
1 CONT the rule of his successors was stabilized through implementing his measures.
