0 @N6000000002188376645@ NOTE Charles the Bold
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles the Bold
1 CONT Duke of Burgundy, Brabant, Guelders, Limburg, Lothier and Luxembourg, Margrave of Namur, Count of Artois, Charolais, Flanders, Hainault, Holland, Zeeland and Zutphen, Count Palatine of Burgundy
1 CONT Rogier van der Weyden painted Charles the Bold in about 1460, wearing the Order of the Golden Fleece
1 CONT Reign 15 June 1467–5 January 1477
1 CONT Full name Charles Martin de Bourgogne
1 CONT Titles Duke of Burgundy, Count of Artois, Flanders, Count Palatine of Burgundy, &c
1 CONT (15 June 1467–5 January 1477)
1 CONT Count of Charolais (1433–5 January 1477)
1 CONT Duke of Guelders, Count of Zutphen (23 February 1473–5 January 1477)
1 CONT Born 21 November 1433
1 CONT Birthplace Dijon, Burgundy
1 CONT Died 5 January 1477
1 CONT Place of death Nancy, Lorraine
1 CONT Predecessor Philip the Good
1 CONT Successor Mary the Rich
1 CONT Consort Catherine of France (1428–1446)
1 CONT Isabella of Bourbon (1436–1465)
1 CONT Margaret of York (1446–1503)
1 CONT Offspring Mary (1457–1482)
1 CONT Royal House House of Valois
1 CONT Father Philip the Good (1396-1467)
1 CONT Mother Isabel of Portugal (1397-1471)
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles the Bold or Charles the Rash (French: Charles le Téméraire)[1] (21 November 1433 – 5 January 1477), baptised Charles Martin, was Duke of Burgundy from 1467 to 1477.
1 CONT
1 CONT Known as Charles the Terrible to his enemies[2], he was the last Valois Duke of Burgundy and his early death was a pivotal, if under-recognised, moment in European history.
1 CONT
1 CONT After his death, his domains began an inevitable slide towards division between France and the Habsburgs (who through marriage to his heiress Mary of Burgundy became his heirs). Neither side was satisfied with the results and the 
1 CONC disintegration of the Burgundian state was a factor in most major wars in Western Europe for over two centuries.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 History
1 CONT           o 1.1 Early life and family
1 CONT           o 1.2 Early battles
1 CONT           o 1.3 Treaty of Péronne
1 CONT           o 1.4 Domestic policies
1 CONT           o 1.5 Building a kingdom
1 CONT           o 1.6 Downfall
1 CONT           o 1.7 Death at Nancy
