0 @N6000000002240794110@ NOTE Charles gave reign to an ambition to make Burgundy independent of France and
1 CONT to raise it, if possible, to a kingdom, and he was almost successful, until
1 CONT 1474. There was even a royal insignia ready and the ceremony arranged when
1 CONT Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor had promised to crown him King of Burgundy.
1 CONT Somehow, Frederick, possibly suspicious of the ambitious Charles, fled into
1 CONT the night. Then on January 5, 1477, a battle was fought outside Nancy, and
1 CONT Charles was killed; his mutilated body was discovered some days later.
