0 @N6000000000438410365@ NOTE Ref; AFN: 9VCN-61 Thomas "Of Plumstead" Hobar Ref; English Martyrology, Abridges from Fox- Book 3, Chapter 14. Reference made to a Thomas Highbed as "Thomas the Martyr" Refused to recant his Protestantism. Was one of 300 burned at
1 CONC  thestake on May 26, 1555. Essex, England. Ref; "The Ancestors and Descendants ofRev. Henry Clark. C.C. VanDauenter 1902." States Thomas Hubbard, Grandfather of Samuel was a gentlemen residing at Hornden-on-the-Hill, in Essex, Eng
1 CONC land a man of good estate and great determination, and zealous and religious in the true service of God. Discovered by an imformer to Bishop Bonner, Thomas was seized, imprisoned and burned at the Stake May 26, 1555. Some records 
1 CONC have death asJanuary 17, 1600, cause; Burned at Stake. Ref; Personal thoughts , Two Thomas's born same family with both alive? Need more research, as to this Thomas? Married Audrey Hare Br, 1541 in Plumstead, England? futher resea
1 CONC rch needed.
