0 @N6000000002322332008@ NOTE He fought a losing battle to keep his Roman Catholic Empire together in the
1 CONT face of Protestantism. He was Charles I of Spain, Charles V as Holy Roman
1 CONT Emperor and King of Germany (1520). He abdicated his Spainish claim to son
1 CONT Philip II and the Holy Roman Empire to brother Ferdinand, retiring to a
1 CONT monastery. Originally, he inherited a Spanish/Habsburg empire that extended
1 CONT 'cross Europe from Spain and the Netherlands to Austria & the kingdom of
1 CONT Naples, and, on into Spanish America. Note: Spain included Sicily.
